<p>Russian Security Council Secretary Sergei Shoigu said Thursday that Moscow is establishing a &quot;full-fledged partnership&quot; with Afghanistan&#x27;s Taliban government and is urging other countries in the region to expand cooperation with Kabul. Shoigu spoke at a meeting of security officials from the Shanghai Cooperation Organisation, a 10-member grouping that includes China, India, Iran, Pakistan and several former Soviet states. Interfax said he also called for the SCO to revive its Afghanistan contact group.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/3t8Evl9Xx4BpigNKC5iDnTt4U5CU8DVnbVr1A4dO-RhiD7TfNwUBeVNij2J2vpwd6WZHkoKNI0d0uSs17BvRzbOUqdovZoWB1WykarR5GHzL4JyLIT_EvFIDuatujZTRjCoQLTvijeh8mjVDUVASixeUbLs_I84x6MPxr3NiLPmTQTRXA4Ns7J_vyFPyM25z83dKk86ObIV-7E53mCrKcmo3QA' alt='Afghanistan and Russian delegations meet at Chahar Chinar Palace in Kabul on Nov. 25, 2024, according to a Taliban deputy prime minister&#x27;s office handout described by Independent Urdu.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Security rationale: Russia says it needs to work with Kabul as it faces threats from militant groups operating in countries from Afghanistan to the Middle East.</li><li>Cooperation scope: Shoigu said the planned dialogue would cover security, trade, cultural ties and humanitarian cooperation rather than recognition alone.</li></ul><blockquote>Full-fledged partnership - Sergei Shoigu</blockquote><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/2000197/russia-establishing-full-partnership-with-afghan-taliban'>Russia establishing &#x27;full partnership&#x27; with Afghan Taliban</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1tcsi8j/russia_says_its_establishing_full_partnership/'>Russia says it&#x27;s establishing full partnership with Afghan Taliban</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/russia-says-its-establishing-full-partnership-with-afghan-taliban'>Russia says it&#x27;s establishing &#x27;full part